    "body": "**Draft, for inspection only. Not meant to merge:** this branch is a hypothetical integration built to answer one question, and it contains merges of four other open PRs.\n\n## What this is\n\ndev + Modules II parts 1 and 2 (#2493 signature types and module values, #2494 width subtyping) + the HTML substrate (#2115) + the livelit stack (#2411 user-defined livelits, #2488 expansion typing, #2489 error dedup), with two follow-ups on top:\n\n1. **The livelit code ported to real modules.** A livelit definition's `Model`, `Action` and `Expansion` are read as manifest type members of the signature `ModuleHelpers.module_sig_type` synthesizes; the livelit branch's own `collect_type_exports` and its labeled-tuple type-export injection in the `Let` case are gone. At runtime `LivelitProj.record_field` reads `ModVal` bindings by name from the evaluated `Module`. Two small changes; they are what user-livelits will need once Modules II lands.\n\n2. **Prototype: the HTML substrate as opt-in modules.** hazel-html's ~120 global constructor names and seven global type aliases (`HTML`, `Attr`, `Cmd`, `Sub`, `App`, `KeyEvent`, `MouseEvent`) become four builtin module values `Html`, `Attr`, `Cmd`, `Sub` (`BuiltinsADT.HtmlModules`). Members are the constructors as snake_case functions, types are `Html.T`, `Attr.T`, `Cmd.T`, `Sub.T`, `Html.App`, `Attr.KeyEvent`, `Attr.MouseEvent`:\n\n   ```\n   Html.div([Attr.style([(\"color\", \"red\")])], [Html.text(\"hi\")])\n   let view = fun m : Model -> ... : Html.T\n   ```\n\n   Constructor names are unchanged, so the renderer and MVU runtime are untouched. Motivation: a user module named `App` lost its type members to the builtin alias `App`, because `Typ.path_sig` tries type aliases before variables. With the modules it works.\n\n## Performance\n\nThe naive module version was 3-4x slower than the global one. Four fixes, each at its source, bring it within ~15%:\n\n- `sig_project_value` / `sig_project_type` substitute into the requested member only, instead of closing the whole signature to read one member.\n- For a builtin module, a member's type keeps `T` as the path `Html.T` (`Typ.sig_project_value_along`), and `meet` accepts two equal paths without normalizing either.\n- `normalize_ctr_type` keeps a builtin-module path compact, as it kept `Var(\"HTML\")`.\n- A builtin module's member elaborates directly to the constructor it denotes; otherwise the evaluator substitutes the whole module value into every closure that names `Html` (80 copies in one program's output).\n\n| nutrient-rotation.hz | baseline (global names) | naive modules | final |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `cli analyze` | 2.3 s | 8.1 s | 2.8 s |\n| `cli run` | 2.75 s | 11 s | 3.1 s |\n| printed output | 181 KB | 1.3 MB | 181 KB |\n\n## Verified\n\n- All 14 MVU and livelit example programs type-check in the qualified form (ported, along with the docs, `Test_MVU` and `Test_UserLivelits`).\n- 1370 tests across MVU, UserLivelits, Modules, Statics, Evaluator, Equality, Elaboration, Menhir, FastParse, Unicode pass. The three tests pinning the compact `Var(\"HTML\")` annotation are removed: that fast path applied only to global aliases.\n- In the browser: the MVU counter renders and counts on clicks, the slider livelit renders and updates with its expansion type check passing, and the Modules slide's item 9 (module named `App`) no longer errors.\n\n## Known gaps\n\n- The projectors doc slide reports type errors around the builtin `^^sliderf` and `^^text` livelits; those lines were not touched here and the errors predate the prototype (they belong to the merge, not the modules design).\n- Bare `Int(x)` still type-checks because JSON's constructor `Int` is still global, so a missed port is silent. Same collision in miniature.\n- Path-preserving projection and constructor elaboration apply only to builtin modules (variables with `Id.invalid`); user modules keep Modules II's manifest substitution.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
